--- b8 medium.en: Move number two is the waiver, and it has no deadline. The manual says you may ask at any time, when the notice arrives, at the same time as your appeal, after the deductions have started, even after the whole debt is collected, and even after an earlier request was denied. If the waiver is approved, the agency may refund what it already withheld. You ask on form SSA-632-BK by mail, by fax, at the office, or by uploading it in your My Social Security account.
