--- b14 medium.en: What happens if you do nothing? The deductions begin on their own, up to 50% of the check. If you are no longer receiving benefits, the agency can keep your federal tax refund, and it can report an unpaid debt to the credit bureaus, which can lead to a denied loan. One exception covers every move. When the agency finds fraud or similar fault, it will not approve a lower rate or a waiver. For everyone else, even the smallest move beats silence. And now, the twist about that April date.
